<title>USA: Clinton 'delighted' by Senate budget move- McCurry.</title>
<headline>Clinton 'delighted' by Senate budget move- McCurry.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton was &quot;delighted&quot; with the progress of a balanced budget agreement in the U.S. Senate, White House spokesman Mike McCurry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The president is delighted that a balanced budget agreement that will cover five million uninsured children and preserve $16 billion to do so is moving toward final passage in the Senate,&quot; McCurry told reporters.</p>
</text>
